[E0005] Error: number literal has a leading zero
   ╭─[ err/04_number_literals/main.wip:5:13 ]
   │
 5 │     val a = 007
   │             ─┬─
   │              ╰─── leading zero
   │
   │ Help: remove the leading zeros: `7`
   │
   │ Note: in C a leading zero makes a literal octal; Wip rejects it so the literal means the same thing to every reader, and writes octal `0o755`
───╯
[E0004] Error: expected a digit after the decimal point
   ╭─[ err/04_number_literals/main.wip:6:13 ]
   │
 6 │     val b = 1.
   │             ─┬
   │              ╰── float literal needs a fractional part
   │
   │ Help: add a zero: `1.0`
───╯
[E0007] Error: invalid suffix `abc` on number literal
   ╭─[ err/04_number_literals/main.wip:7:15 ]
   │
 7 │     val c = 12abc
   │               ─┬─
   │                ╰─── not part of the number
   │
   │ Help: a number cannot run into a name; separate them with an operator
───╯
[E0007] Error: invalid suffix `e` on number literal
   ╭─[ err/04_number_literals/main.wip:8:14 ]
   │
 8 │     val d = 3e
   │              ┬
   │              ╰── not part of the number
   │
   │ Help: an exponent needs digits: `3e0`
───╯
